{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790964237,"nonce":"OYNgIPXyf8gq5zCIQalX9yhM7TE=","title":"Embed: a host calls a function value the program made","message":"A function value crosses to an embedder as a dynamic value under FUNC_TAG, a record whose first item is the code's address and second its arity word (zyntax_builtins::functions). zyntax_embed::foreign could read a foreign object, a tuple and a number, but gave the host no way to call a function value, so a closure a program returns (Python's `lambda x: x + k`) could not be called by the embedding host. Caribou needs it for a Python closure crossing out to Haxe and Wren.\n\nzyntax_embed::foreign gains FUNC_TAG, MAX_CALL_ARITY, is_function, function_arity (least, most from the arity word) and call_function, which calls the code as zb_call_n does: the record, then each argument as a dynamic value, to a dynamic result. A call passes every argument the code takes, since leaving one out for its default needs the frontend's missing-argument marker, and a variadic code needs the library to pack its list; both are refused with a TypeError.","files":null}]}